==============================================================================
A  The Kaplan-Meier value of J28 against the bearing-averaged, labeled-healthy rate
==============================================================================
  J28 censors a non-firing trajectory at u = 1. An alarm needs c = 3 confirming records, so i* <= n - 3
  and every observed onset fraction U = i*/n is below 1: all censoring falls after the last event.
  Kaplan-Meier on [0, 1] then reduces to the empirical survival function with the censored trajectories
  counted as 'not yet fired':  S(u) = #{j : U_j > u} / N  for u < 1.
  Its restricted mean on [0, 1] is  (1/N) [ sum_fired U_j + N_censored ],  so
      1 - RMST = (1/N) sum_fired (1 - U_j),
  which is the bearing-averaged positive rate with non-firing trajectories labeled healthy.
  largest observed onset fraction over the 294 firing pairs: 0.9875 (< 1, as the argument needs)
  cells checked (J28 reports datasets with >= 3 trajectories): 21; largest |KM - bearing-averaged healthy| = 2.78e-16
  PASS: equal to 1e-09 in every cell. Kaplan-Meier is not a third treatment for this quantity.

